            <div xml:id="d353">

                <pb facs="0562" n="438" xml:id="pg438"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00/2674: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Morales</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-08-30T09:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 30,
                                1923—9 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 31—9:50
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>74. Referring to the Department’s telegram of August 28, 7 p.m. The President
                    informed me that he was willing to assure the candidates that he would not
                    impose a candidate at the forthcoming elections and would do everything within
                    his power to guarantee free elections. …</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morales</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
